# The GPUIX source update.sh builds: Kybern's fork of remorses/gpuix, whose
# `kybern` branch is the upstream release in `upstream` plus our commits. Its
# zed submodule points at Tresnanda/zed's `kybern` branch (the GPUI commits).
# A native change is a commit on those branches and a new pin here; see
# README.md, "Changing the native module".
repo=https://github.com/Tresnanda/gpuix.git
# CI triage: the heads of the forks' `ci-fix` branches: `next` (WP1 + WP10 Windows)
# plus the Linux screenshot through a wgpu readback and KYBERN_ROUNDED_CLIP=0 keeping
# edge fades, until they are merged into `kybern`; then pin the merged kybern heads.
# WP5 (notifications): the forks' `wp5` branches, one commit each on top of that.
commit=87797905da10596ea9a51712dbea4be4a133779b
# The zed submodule commit `commit` records; update.sh refuses a checkout that differs.
zed=fa96d835c5acd417e7f53c7b8f3730c61766c6ab
# The upstream tag `commit` is based on. It must be `@gpuix/native@<VERSION>`.
upstream=@gpuix/native@0.11.0
